<Programs>
<Program Name="MainProgram" TestEdits="false" MainRoutineName="MainRoutine" FaultRoutineName="Fault_Routine" Disabled="false">
<Tags/>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Fault_Routine" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung grabs the fault record for the program and stores it in a tag created with a user defined structure.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(PROGRAM,THIS,MAJORFAULTRECORD,FaultRecord.TimeLow);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="MainRoutine" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
All information provided  -- No warranty or implied merchantability.
Refer to the RSLogix 5000 End User License Agreement (EULA) in the Release Notes.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This program shows how to read from the CPU Chassis Information.

This rung executes once when the processor changes from program to run mode to determine if the program is loaded into a specific processor.

The S:FS bit is set for one scan each time the program transitions from program to run mode.
The MSG instruction performs a CIP Generic read operation to the controllers backplane object.  The attributes for this operation are:
	Service Code = 1 (Get Attributes All)
	Class Name = 66 (Backplane Object)
	Instance Name = 1 (Primary Instance)
	Attribute Name = left blank
	Source = left blank
	Number of elements = 0
	Destination = Tag to store 18 bytes of information
	Path = 1,x  (Where x is the slot number for the controller in the chassis)
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(S:FS)MSG(Read_Backplane_Info);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung validates the information that is received from the backplane object on the controller.

If the backplane serial number, backplane size, or processor slot do not match the appropriate settings, the JSR to the fault routine initiates a shutdown of the processor with fault type 04 and code 01, both of which are unknown to the software.

Remove the AFI instruction to execute the rungs logic on this rung.
 ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[AFI()XIC(Read_Backplane_Info.DN)[NEQ(Backplane_Info.SERIAL_NO,Saved_Backplane_Serial_No) ,NEQ(Backplane_Info.MOD_ADDR,Saved_Backplane_Slot) ,NEQ(Backplane_Info.SIZE,Saved_Backplane_Size) ]JSR(Fault_Routine,1,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
</Programs>
